<!-- #region q2 -->

**Iteration 1** (w = 0, b = 0):

| x | y | ŷ = wx + b | e = ŷ − y | e·x |
|:-:|:-:|--:|--:|--:|
| 1 | 3 | 0 | −3 | −3 |
| 2 | 5 | 0 | −5 | −10 |
| 3 | 7 | 0 | −7 | −21 |
|  |  | **Σ** | **−15** | **−34** |

$$ \begin{aligned} \frac{\partial J}{\partial w} &= \tfrac{2}{3}(-34) = -22.6667, & w &\leftarrow 0 - 0.05(-22.6667) = \mathbf{1.1333} \\ \frac{\partial J}{\partial b} &= \tfrac{2}{3}(-15) = -10, & b &\leftarrow 0 - 0.05(-10) = \mathbf{0.5} \end{aligned} $$

**Iteration 2** (w = 1.1333, b = 0.5):

| x | y | ŷ = wx + b | e = ŷ − y | e·x |
|:-:|:-:|--:|--:|--:|
| 1 | 3 | 1.6333 | −1.3667 | −1.3667 |
| 2 | 5 | 2.7667 | −2.2333 | −4.4667 |
| 3 | 7 | 3.9 | −3.1 | −9.3 |
|  |  | **Σ** | **−6.7** | **−15.1333** |

$$ \begin{aligned} \frac{\partial J}{\partial w} &= \tfrac{2}{3}(-15.1333) = -10.0889, & w &\leftarrow 1.1333 - 0.05(-10.0889) = \mathbf{1.6378} \\ \frac{\partial J}{\partial b} &= \tfrac{2}{3}(-6.7) = -4.4667, & b &\leftarrow 0.5 - 0.05(-4.4667) = \mathbf{0.7233} \end{aligned} $$

MSE: 27.6667 → 1.0897. The data lies on y = 2x + 1, so the steps are heading towards w = 2, b = 1.

